ure#5-shared-rails--same-infra-different-products","content":"Vault (`roadmap-index.md` + `future-improvements.md`)"},"245":{"id":"/docs/architecture-164","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#5-shared-rails--same-infra-different-products","content":"Vault (`roadmap-index.md` + `future-improvements.md`)"},"246":{"id":"/docs/architecture-165","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#5-shared-rails--same-infra-different-products","content":"Vault (read-only)"},"247":{"id":"/docs/architecture-166","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#5-shared-rails--same-infra-different-products","content":"**Linear** (`B-Unit` project, workspace `EVE`)"},"248":{"id":"/docs/architecture-167","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#5-shared-rails--same-infra-different-products","content":"**The spine is Hermes.** Newfin and Rodyna are fully independent repos with their own Supabase projects and deploys — they'd run without Jackie-OS. What ties the ecosystem together: Hermes owns the morning/journal cron, is the **LLM gateway** (live: `gpt-5.6-sol` + DeepSeek cron profile), and runs named Newfin workers (`/intel`, deep research). The vault never holds code — only *knowledge about* the repos; each repo's `docs/solutions/` holds the technical learnings, indexed back into `Vault/Agent-Learnings/`."},"249":{"id":"/docs/architecture-168","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Concepts / vocabulary:** Concepts (Hermes, two-bot model, three-cron system, LLM gateway, Linear integration)."},"250":{"id":"/docs/architecture-169","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Operating rules / read-order:** CLAUDE.md (local), Vault/CLAUDE.md (local)."},"251":{"id":"/docs/architecture-170","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Cron inventory + Mac↔VPS parity:** Vault Rhythm."},"252":{"id":"/docs/architecture-171","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Operator cheat-sheet:** Cheat Sheet."},"253":{"id":"/docs/architecture-172","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Per-project architecture:** each project has `ARCHITECTURE.md` (Jackie-OS root, `~/dev/{newfin,rodyna,bunit,draw}/`) — read before working in that project."},"254":{"id":"/docs/architecture-173","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Linear tracking:** execute in Cursor. History: Desk journey."},"255":{"id":"/docs/architecture-174","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Draw:** Draw repo `ARCHITECTURE.md`"},"256":{"id":"/docs/architecture-175","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#pointers","content":"**Visual version (human-facing):** docs site \"The system map\" page."},"257":{"id":"/docs/catalog","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"page","content":"System Catalog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Look it up"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog"},"258":{"id":"/docs/catalog-0","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog","content":"Every skill and script in Jackie-OS — the map to navigate the system."},"259":{"id":"/docs/catalog-1","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"Skills vs Scripts — decision"},"260":{"id":"/docs/catalog-2","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"How it fits together (30-second orientation)"},"261":{"id":"/docs/catalog-3","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Skills — grouped by job"},"262":{"id":"/docs/catalog-4","page_id":"/docs/catalog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/catalog#what-runs-when-cron","content":"What runs when (cron)"},"263":{"id":"/docs/catalog-5","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog","content":"> **The map.** Every skill (what the AI does) and script (what runs on a schedule or on demand). Start here to navigate the system. Depth links: skills → Skills Registry; what-runs-when → Hermes VPS crontab + Vault Rhythm; operating → Cheat Sheet."},"264":{"id":"/docs/catalog-6","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Skills** are LLM judgment playbooks — markdown decision trees that agents follow when running a task (example: `morning-brief.md` = what a brief contains, how to read vault/email, when to alert, how to publish). Skills are the AI's **thinking layer**; they live in `System/skills/` and the agent reads them whole, then improvises per context."},"265":{"id":"/docs/catalog-7","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Scripts** are the mechanics layer — bash or Python executables that handle scheduling, filesystem operations, subprocess calls, and state management (example: `morning-brief-vps.py` = pull vault, run the skill in the Hermes sandbox, format output, write to file, deliver). Scripts live in `System/{coo,capture,ops,periodic,work,lib,scripts}/` and are the **source of truth** — edits go here, never the VPS copy (symlinked)."},"266":{"id":"/docs/catalog-8","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills-vs-scripts--decision","content":"**Pattern:** Skills call scripts (or describe the sequence scripts follow). A typical cron job is a thin `&#60;name>.sh` wrapper (cron entry) that execs a `&#60;name>.py` (logic). When the LLM is involved, it's one `hermes -z` call returning text that the script writes."},"267":{"id":"/docs/catalog-9","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Skills** = markdown playbooks the AI (Claude/Hermes) follows. Some are agent-run (judgment), some are implemented mechanically by a script."},"268":{"id":"/docs/catalog-10","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Scripts** = the executable layer. They live in the repo under `System/{coo,capture,ops,periodic,work,lib,scripts}/` and are the **source of truth**. On the VPS they're symlinked into `~/.hermes/scripts/` by `hermes-vps-link-scripts.sh` (rebuilt on every autodeploy `git pull`). &#x2A;*Edit the repo copy, never the VPS copy.**"},"269":{"id":"/docs/catalog-11","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Two schedulers:** the **Hermes agent-cron** (`~/.hermes/cron/jobs.json`, edited via the dashboard — the morning stack) and the **OS crontab** (`hermes-vps-crontab.txt` — deploy/health/weekly)."},"270":{"id":"/docs/catalog-12","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#how-it-fits-together-30-second-orientation","content":"**Pattern:** most cron jobs are a thin `&#60;name>.sh` wrapper (cron entry) that execs a `&#60;name>.py` (the logic). `no_agent` jobs are mechanical; the LLM, when used, is one `hermes -z` call returning text that the Python writes."},"271":{"id":"/docs/catalog-13","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Full registry: Skills Registry."},"272":{"id":"/docs/catalog-14","page_id":"/docs/catalog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/catalog#skills--grouped-by-job","content":"Skill"},"273":{"id":"/docs/catalog-15","page_id":"/docs/catalog","t