":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/concepts#what-lives-where-post-2026-06-29-restructure","content":"What lives where (post-2026-06-29 restructure)"},"482":{"id":"/docs/concepts-16","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts","content":"> Shared domain vocabulary for this project — entities, named processes, and status concepts with project-specific meaning. Seeded with core domain vocabulary, then accretes as learnings; direct edits are fine. Glossary only, not a spec or catch-all."},"483":{"id":"/docs/concepts-17","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**hot.md** — A \\~500-word cache in `Vault/hot.md` of current focus and open loops, refreshed at every session end; fastest orientation for any agent starting a new session."},"484":{"id":"/docs/concepts-18","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**wrap-up** — The wrap-up skill that syncs the vault, updates `## Status` in project notes, refreshes `hot.md`, and commits."},"485":{"id":"/docs/concepts-19","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**brief** — An AI-generated daily or period summary (morning brief, weekly brief) that reads code activity, vault status, and calendar to inform the day."},"486":{"id":"/docs/concepts-20","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**skill** — A repeatable workflow playbook (markdown + optional code) living in `System/skills/`; an AI reads it and executes the defined steps. Global owned skills carry the `jos-` prefix (see Skills Registry)."},"487":{"id":"/docs/concepts-21","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**Hermes** — The always-on VPS agent that runs the scheduled tasks and sync loop while your Mac is off."},"488":{"id":"/docs/concepts-22","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**Persik** — Two Telegram bots: `@Persik_finbot` (the Newfin-hosted product bot) and `@persik_hermes_bot` (the full Hermes VPS channel)."},"489":{"id":"/docs/concepts-23","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**workers (retired 2026-08-07)** — The Cyrus/Buzz named fleet (Fablio / Cursorio / Codexio / Cyrusio / Marketio / Scriptio) is off. Interactive coding is **Cursor**. Linear is tracking only. History: Desk journey."},"490":{"id":"/docs/concepts-24","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**desk** — Live stack: Cursor + Tailscale + Hermes VPS + Grokbot. Contract: Operator desk. bb is not in active use."},"491":{"id":"/docs/concepts-25","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#core-terms--used-daily","content":"**registry** — The `System/project-registry.md` file that maps each project to its code repo and/or STATUS file, serving as the single source of truth for sync."},"492":{"id":"/docs/concepts-26","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#occasional","content":"**janitor** — An OKF linter and maintenance tool that audits frontmatter compliance and keeps the vault structure clean (quarterly cron)."},"493":{"id":"/docs/concepts-27","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#occasional","content":"**docs-first** — Before building anything new, check the master index for prior art; on ship, update the owning doc in the same commit."},"494":{"id":"/docs/concepts-28","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#deprecated--winding-down","content":"**Cowork** — The Claude desktop app's scheduled-tasks harness on Sergei's Mac. **Effectively retired** — a single leftover schedule remains (Sunday 18:00 weekly-review); everything else runs on the VPS."},"495":{"id":"/docs/concepts-29","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#deprecated--winding-down","content":"**Bases/Ops board** — Obsidian Bases kanban for task tracking. **Being replaced by Linear** (migration in progress: B-Unit, Newfin, Rodyna already on Linear; Jackie-OS itself deliberately stays on Bases/markdown)."},"496":{"id":"/docs/concepts-30","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#jackie-os-agent-any-editor-hermes-optional","content":"Jackie OS is portable files — the vault, the skills, the rules. **Primary interactive desk is Cursor** (Operator desk). Hosts talk over **Tailscale**. Opening `~/Jackie-OS` (or a `~/dev/*` project) in Cursor — or Claude Code / Codex — auto-reads `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` and runs the skills that live inside it. `wrap up` from any session syncs the vault, `## Status`, and `hot.md`, then commits. **Hermes** (below) is the always-on automation instance on the VPS. **Grokbot** is a parallel chat surface, not the desk of record. bb is not in active use."},"497":{"id":"/docs/concepts-31","page_id":"/docs/concepts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/concepts#okf-open-knowledge-format-bundle","content":"Jackie-OS adopts **Open Knowledge Format** *frontmatter* — every skill, solution, concept, project note, daily, and brief carries structured YAML (`type`, `title`, `timestamp`, …). This makes the vault a **portable, vendor-neutral knowledge bundle**: anyone can fork the structure and wire a different automation layer, and any agent can orient and retrieve by metadata instead of inferring from prose. **Frontmatter only** — internal links stay as Obsidian wikilinks (OKF's relative-link convention is *not* adopted). Backfilled by `System/tools/add-okf-frontmatter.py`; enforced by `janitor` OKF lint mode. Headline goal = portability; faster agent orientation/retrieval is the day-to-day payoff."},