t":"—"},"1178":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-114","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**Task tracking (Linear)** — team `EVE`, workspace `evegelin`. `bunit` + `b-unit` share the **B-Unit** product project (backlog + agent loop, `Pipeline` = `dev`/`content`/`research`); the TikTok/marketing production pipeline lives in a separate **B-Unit — Content** project (episode-per-issue, milestones = weeks). Labels are one workspace-wide 3-group taxonomy — `Pipeline` · `Stage` (needs-refinement/needs-approval) · `Type` (Bug/Feature/Improvement) — shared by every project, nothing to recreate per repo. The active code portfolio, including **Draw**, is tracked in Linear. Non-code projects remain in Bases."},"1179":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-115","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**Tracker switch (`tracker: linear | bases`)** — the per-project flag that project-sync and morning-brief branch on. Default is `bases` for **every** row (task state from `git`/`status-file` + the Obsidian Ops Bases, exactly as before — no change). A row flips to `linear` once its Linear board exists: its task/plan state is then read from Linear via `System/scripts/linear-fetch.py` (`--project &#60;Linear project name>`) **instead of** the Ops Bases, closing the \"Linear-only work invisible until /wrap-up\" gap (esp. `content`/`research` issues with no PR). Migrate one row at a time; flip back to `bases` to revert."},"1180":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-116","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**`tracker: linear`** → `jackie-os` → Jackie OS project; `b-unit`, `bunit` → B-Unit; `rodyna` → Rodyna; `newfin` → Newfin; `sergeichan` → Personal Website; `draw` → Draw (agent-team enabled; routing label `Draw`)."},"1181":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-117","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**`tracker: bases`** → every other active row (default; unchanged behavior)."},"1182":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-118","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"**Source types**"},"1183":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-119","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"Source"},"1184":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-120","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"Truth"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-121","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"Sync direction"},"1186":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-122","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`git`"},"1187":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-123","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`origin/&#60;branch>` + local clone health"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-124","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"repo → vault `## Status`; optional mirror → `STATUS.md`"},"1189":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-125","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`status-file`"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-126","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`Projects/*/STATUS.md`"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-127","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"STATUS → vault `## Status`; vault one-liner → mirror footer"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-128","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"`vault`"},"1193":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-129","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"vault note file in Jackie-OS git"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-130","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry","content":"jackie-os git log on that file → vault `## Status` (dormant projects)"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-131","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"A `git` row whose **GitHub** cell carries 🤝 (or whose Source shows `⚠️ shared`) is a repo Sergei **does not own** — e.g. `AleannLab/draw`, co-owned with a collaborator. For these repos:"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-132","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Default is READ-ONLY.** project-sync may diff `origin/&#60;branch>` → update the vault `## Status` and `STATUS.md` mirror. It must not push, commit, branch, or open a PR on a shared repo unless Sergei explicitly authorizes that repository."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-133","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Draw exception (authorized 2026-07-12):** `AleannLab/draw` is an active Linear agent-team code project. A delegated agent may implement an issue in an isolated worktree and open a normal reviewable PR; do not push directly to `main`. This exception applies only to Draw, not other shared rows."},"1198":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-134","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**No Jackie-OS scaffolding.** Never add `docs/JACKIE-OS.md`, `docs/solutions/`, an Agent-Learnings `## Jackie-OS sync` paragraph in the repo's `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`, or any other Jackie-OS bookkeeping file. Bridge/learnings/compound write-ups stay on the Jackie-OS side only (vault note + `Vault/Agent-Learnings/{Title} learnings.md`). Skipped because: any PR there lands in the collaborator's repo."},"1199":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-135","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Merge-poll:** owned repos are covered by the central Action in jackie-os (registry-driven). No per-repo sync tokens or Cursor automations."},"1200":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-136","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"Only **actual app changes** Sergei makes himself belong in a shared repo — never agent housekeeping."},"1201":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-137","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Add a row** when a project gets a vault note — never hardcode paths in skills. &#x2A;*New project (code or non-code):** run skill Add a Project (registry + vault + **plans scaffold** + bridge + learnings + poller registration)."},"1202":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-138","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Plans surface (owned code repos):** every new owned repo gets `plans/roadmap-index.md` + `plans/future-improvements.md` at onboarding. Non-code projects get `Projects/{Name}/plans/`. After each ship: wrap-up § Catalog cleanup."},"1203":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-139","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#write-policy--shared--contribute-only-repos-","content":"**Code-repo bridge:** each **owned** `git` row should have `docs/JACKIE-OS.md` in the repo (template: `System/templates/JACKIE-OS-bridge.md`) so Cursor/Claude Code sessions know to run project-sync from Jackie-OS at session end. **Shared repos (🤝) get NO bridge** — see Write policy above."},"1204":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-140","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Use these when writing skills, bridge docs, or Agent-Learnings catalogs. Registry **Path** column uses the Mac home form; agents on other machines substitute."},"1205":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-141","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Context"},"1206":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-142","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Jackie-OS root"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-143","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Example code repo"},"1208":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-144","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Mac (Sergei)**"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-145","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`~/Jackie-OS/`"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-146","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`~/dev/newfin/`"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-147","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Linux / Cursor cloud**"},"1212":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-148","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`/workspace/` (or clone path)"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-149","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Must exist locally for `git` rows — see cloud note below"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-150","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Install guide default**"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-151","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"`~/jackie-os/`"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-152","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"Any path you choose; update registry"},"1217":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-153","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Branch defaults:** jackie-os → `master`; all code repos → `main`."},"1218":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-154","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Cloud / headless agents:** Cursor cloud and CI clones often contain only Jackie-OS. Code repos live in a sibling tree (`~/dev/`), not checked out in cloud — project-sync skips missing paths and flags them; it does not fail the whole sync. For full sync, clones must exist at registry paths on the machine running sync (typically Sergei's Mac via Cowork or wrap-up)."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-155","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Mac auto-pull (`~/Jackie-OS` + `~/dev`):** LaunchAgent `com.jackie.dev-repos-pull` — every 30m + login; registry-driven ff-only pull (Jackie-OS `master` first, then code repos; skips dirty trees). Install: `bash System/scripts/dev-repos-pull-install.sh install`. Log: `~/.hermes/logs/dev-repos-pull.log`. Manual before a long session: `bash System/scripts/dev-repos-pull.sh`."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/project-registry-156","page_id":"/docs/project-registry","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/project-registry#canonical-paths","content":"**Agent-Learnings catalogs:** prefer registry `Path` + relative `docs/solutions/` over hardcoded Mac absolutes."},"1221":{"id":"/docs/roadmap","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"page","content":"Roadmap — Active Plans","breadcrumbs":["Docs","What's the plan?"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-0","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"Current forward work, shipped ledger, and tracking status."},"1223":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-1","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#roadmap--active-plans","content":"Roadmap — Active Plans"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-2","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#active-plans","content":"Active Plans"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-3","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#shipped","content":"Shipped"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-4","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#roadmap--active-plans","content":"This page shows the current roadmap for Jackie-OS and related projects. Plans are tracked here as dated initiatives; shipped items move to the **Shipped** section. The source of truth lives in code repos' `plans/roadmap-index.md` files and this file for Jackie-OS itself."},"1227":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-5","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#roadmap--active-plans","content":"**Key principle:** forward work lives in this file while active; upon ship, the plan is documented in the ledger, the dated plan file is deleted from git (`git rm`), and any durable decision is captured in the decisions log."},"1228":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-6","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#roadmap--active-plans","content":"See a